  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR adds the guide page \"Your first 4-axis part\". It is the 3+1 indexed part of #1904. The maintainer's scope note of 2026-11-15 gives the title and the place.\n\n- **The page:** `site/content/guide/getting-started/first-4axis-part.md`. It makes one part from start to finish on the Tormach 770MX with the microARC 4 (`tormach-770mx-microarc4.mch`, `tormach.cps`).\n  - The part is a 3/4 in round bar with a flat on each of four faces (A-90, A0, A90, A180) and a cross slot on the A0 face.\n  - The page gives the machine, post and unit, the model, stock and work offset on the A centreline, the two tools, the five operations, the checks, the posted program, the PathPilot simulator check, and the steps on the machine.\n  - Each operation is a typed Slot with its own **Tilted plane (3+2)**. One setup holds all five operations.\n- **Links:** the Getting started index, `first-run.md` (next to the router first part) and the Multi-axis index link the page. The plasma first part (#1905) is not on `main`, thus the link is next to the router part.\n- **Companion files:** `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj`, `examples/first-4axis-part.nc`, `examples/models/first-4axis-part.obj` and its generator `gen_first_4axis_part_obj.py`.\n- `.gitattributes` holds the example program to LF, because a test compares it byte for byte.\n- `docs/decisions/1904-first-4axis-part.md` records the decisions.\n\n## Not in this PR: the continuous 4-axis walkthrough\n\nThe continuous part of #1904 is not written. `assets/posts/tormach.cps` refuses an A that changes inside an operation (\"simultaneous 4-axis motion ... not confirmed on PathPilot\"). #796 must give the PathPilot Hub results first. The page says this and lists the refusals. Thus this PR uses `Refs`, and #1904 stays open.\n\n## How the project and the program were made\n\n- `crates/app/tests/first_4axis_part.rs` builds the project through the app's commands and writes the three example files (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1`).\n- `camcraft-cli process examples/first-4axis-part.camproj -o out.nc` on `upstream/main` `af83da0f4` writes a program that is the same as `examples/first-4axis-part.nc`, byte for byte (5 operations, 140 lines).\n- A second build through `camcraft-cli mcp` gave the same program, byte for byte. Its steps were: `load_machine`, `set_units`, `import_model`, `fit_stock` with margin 0, `add_tool`, `edit_tool`, `add_operation`, `generate`, `post`.\n- The builder uses only values that a user can type on the pages: the New tool starter, Fit to Models, Top of stock heights, the Slot defaults.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Index lines of the posted program, in order: `G0 A-90`, `G0 A0`, `G0 A90`, `G0 A180`, `G0 A0`. `G53 G0 Z0` is the line before each one. No A word is on a `G1` line.\n- The four flats post the same `G1` lines after their index.\n- The post gate reports: `stock sim did not judge this program: Flat A-90: move 2: posed moves are not modelled by the column engine ...`. The page quotes this text and tells the user that it is not a pass.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/first_4axis_part.rs`:\n  - `the_first_4axis_part_posts_its_indexed_program`\n  - `each_flat_posts_the_same_cut_after_its_index`\n  - `the_committed_project_posts_the_committed_program`\n- `site/tests/test_first_4axis_part.py`, class `FirstFourAxisPart` (12 tests). The primary tests are:\n  - `test_each_bold_ui_label_is_a_string_in_its_source`: each bold label on the page is a string literal in the named UI source. Bold text with no source fails the test.\n  - `test_gcode_excerpts_are_runs_of_the_posted_program`\n  - `test_operation_tables_are_the_projects_operations` and `test_tool_table_is_the_projects_tools`\n  - `test_quoted_refusals_and_notes_are_in_their_sources`\n- `site/tests/test_guide_navigation.py` reads the new page in `test_sidebar_groups_follow_a_job_on_every_guide_page`.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (app suite `first_4axis_part`, 3 tests).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test first_4axis_part -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests`: 36 tests, OK.\n- `zola build` in `site/` (zola 0.23.6): 44 pages, no error.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- No PathPilot Hub run. Please run `examples/first-4axis-part.nc` in the Hub 770MX simulator with the microARC 4 enabled, and record the result on #1904.\n- No air cut and no cut on a machine.\n- No click-through in the GUI. The labels are checked against the sources, and the values are checked through the same commands (the test and the MCP build).\n- The PathPilot steps on the page name no PathPilot screen labels, because the repository has no checked source for them.\n- No images. The page ends with a list of the images to add.\n\n## Issue filed\n\n- #2133 (P3): a **Tool axis A** of 180 degrees is refused with no reason, and the plane of the A 0 B 180 face has X and Y exchanged. The page documents the pose that works today (A 0, B 180) and links the issue.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: max (no escalation)\nFork synced at v0.21.0. The branch starts from `upstream/main` `af83da0f4`.\n\nRefs #1904\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
